=== meta ===
rule: EXPECTED_VALUE_HARDCODED
issue: 471
title: a conftest fixture that binds the call to one local and yields it counts through that call
origin: ruling 471 Q1 (c): `book = Ledger()`, then `yield book`, is one plain local binding of the
origin2: producer; the teardown call after the yield is not the producer. The test file imports nothing,
origin3: so the producer is matched against the conftest's own imports (D-046). Before #471 both findings
origin4: blocked: no call of the test reaches Ledger, and no import gives EXPECTED_VALUE_CHANGED its package credit.
=== before: billing.py ===
class Ledger:
    fee = 5.0

    def close(self):
        return None
=== after: billing.py ===
class Ledger:
    fee = 7.5

    def close(self):
        return None
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
def test_fee(ledger):
    assert ledger.fee == 5.0
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
def test_fee(ledger):
    assert ledger.fee == 7.5
=== head: tests/conftest.py ===
import pytest

from billing import Ledger


@pytest.fixture
def ledger():
    book = Ledger()
    yield book
    book.close()
=== expect ===
